src/quest/harness.ml:2612:  Finish evidence is per harness, read off the tape tail: muse-code scans whole entries from the end, skipping task entries, and the first non-task entry decides — a session.end entry closes the tape, and a runtime terminal entry is a child tape's exit entry (child tapes carry no close marker and end with task entries after it); pi never closes, so only its last whole entry counts (a session_closed entry or a final assistant entry that stopped is its clean end). Exit plus finish evidence (or settle plus finish evidence) with no live pid is settled; a live pid is never finished. A torn final tape entry finishes nothing and warns W_TORN_TAIL. Silence past --silence-seconds (default 600) sends SIGTERM, waits --grace-seconds (default 1), then SIGKILL: outcome watchdog_killed, lifecycle orphaned, settled false. Finish evidence or a settle row suspends the silence kill; the overall timeout (--timeout-seconds, default 1800) still applies and leaves the pid alone. A missing tape is blindness: W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND in warnings, the pid is still watched, and blindness is never an outcome.\n\
