./_build/default/src/quest/harness.ml:2592:  Mechanism (mvp.4): each changed tick appends one pointer-only observation row to the Run's own <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl (keyed by run-id; session-id is only an InitRecord field) and refreshes its disposable <run-id>.json cache. Since mvp.5 the derivation logs are the sole lifecycle read path; the retired shared maps are never read or written. Writer discipline (followup.1): each row is a single write() on an O_APPEND descriptor and the cache is a uniquely named temp file in the same directory, fsynced and renamed over the old cache, so parallel supervisors never tear a row or the cache; a torn final line is ignored by the fold and reported as W_TORN_TAIL. Tape binding (followup.3, pinned by followup.4): when the InitRecord names no tape, the first pointer-only tape_binding row in the same log names it, one tape to one Run, never rebound; with no tape at all the probe is blind (W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND) and the lifecycle stays init.\n\
