2589:  Streams NDJSON lifecycle_change rows on stdout, ends with one JSON verdict {ok, quest, outcome, settled, rollup, runs, inbox, orphans}.\n\
2590:  Outcomes and exit classes: settled=0, watchdog_killed=1 (terminal), timeout=3 (retryable), human_gate=4 (needs-human).\n\
2597:  Emits {ok, checks}; a missing or reshaped tape source adds W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND to warnings and never blocks work.\n\
2608:let help_watch = "bp3 harness watch - blocking watch on one Run:\n\
2609:  bp3 harness watch --run-id <id> [--silence-seconds <n>] [--timeout-seconds <n>] [--grace-seconds <n>]\n\
2610:  bp3 harness watch --session-id <id> [--silence-seconds <n>] [--timeout-seconds <n>] [--grace-seconds <n>]\n\
2611:  Engine is derived from the Run InitRecord, never stated. Finds the tape like find-tape, then blocks in code: streams NDJSON lifecycle_change rows and ends with one verdict {ok, run_id, harness, session_id, wal, pid, outcome, settled, lifecycle}.\n\
2612:  Finish evidence is per harness, read off the tape tail: muse-code scans whole entries from the end, skipping task entries, and the first non-task entry decides — a session.end entry closes the tape, and a runtime terminal entry is a child tape's exit entry (child tapes carry no close marker and end with task entries after it); pi never closes, so only its last whole entry counts (a session_closed entry or a final assistant entry that stopped is its clean end). Exit plus finish evidence (or settle plus finish evidence) with no live pid is settled; a live pid is never finished. A torn final tape entry finishes nothing and warns W_TORN_TAIL. Silence past --silence-seconds (default 600) sends SIGTERM, waits --grace-seconds (default 1), then SIGKILL: outcome watchdog_killed, lifecycle orphaned, settled false. Finish evidence or a settle row suspends the silence kill; the overall timeout (--timeout-seconds, default 1800) still applies and leaves the pid alone. A missing tape is blindness: W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND in warnings, the pid is still watched, and blindness is never an outcome.\n\
2614:  Outcomes and exit classes: settled=0, watchdog_killed=1 (terminal), timeout=3 (retryable), human_gate=4 (needs-human).\n\
2615:Example: bp3 harness watch --run-id 20261115T000000Z-handoff-pi-model-c1 --silence-seconds 600\n"
